==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nb|a la mode}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|nb|fr|à la mode||in fashion}}, first part from {{bor|nb|fr|à la||in the [[style]] or [[manner]] of}}. Last part from {{der|nb|fr|mode||fashion, trend}}, from {{der|nb|frm|mode}}, from {{der|nb|fro|mode|g=f}}, from {{der|nb|la|modus|g=m||measure, manner}}, from {{der|nb|itc-pro|*modōs}}, from {{inh|nb|ine-pro||*mod-ōs|measure}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*med-||to measure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nb|/a.laˈmɔːd/}}
* {{audio|nb|NB - Pronunciation of Norwegian Bokmål «à la mode».ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|nb|mɔːd}}
* {{hyphenation|nb|a|la|mode}}
* {{homophones|nb|a la mode}}

===Adverb===
{{head|nb|adverb}}

# {{l|en|à la mode}}, [[fashionable]]; in a particular [[style]] or [[fashion]].
#* {{quote-journal|nb|year=1970|work=Dagbladet|text=her gis ingen konsesjoner til à-la-mode-radikalisme|t=here no licenses are granted for à-la-mode radicalism}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2008|author={{w|Nils Johan Ringdal}}|title=Georg Valentin von Munthe af Morgenstiernes forunderlige liv og reiser|page=43|passage=Bertha trengte naturligvis et utall kjoler – og ingen vet hvor mange hatter – for å kunne kle seg kongelig à la mode til hver middag|t=Bertha naturally needed countless dresses - and no one knows how many hats - to be able to dress royally à la mode for every dinner}}
# [[modern]], the latest [[trend]]
#: ''sangerens bryllup ble et kjendisbryllup à la mode''
#:: the singer's wedding became a celebrity wedding à la mode

